# Read-only tour of the ACME Project Tracker API, for the VS Code "REST Client"
# extension (humao.rest-client). Click "Send Request" above any request.
#
# 1. Run the "login" request first. It asks for the password (nothing secret is
#    stored in this file). Every later request reuses its token, which lasts 15
#    minutes: after that every request answers 401, so run "login" again.
# 2. Pick the server on the @baseUrl line: {{aws}} (live, CloudFront -> Lambda ->
#    Aurora) or {{local}} (needs ./bin/start-dev.sh running, proxy on :3001).
#
# Every path and query name below is taken from backend/tracker/api/routes.py and
# the services. There are no write requests here, so nothing in the data changes.
# (Logging in does not write an audit row: reads and logins are not audited.)

@aws = https://d1gov8jpsxhwer.cloudfront.net/api/tracker
@local = http://localhost:3001/api/tracker
@baseUrl = {{aws}}

@token = {{login.response.body.token}}
# Project 1 is Apollo in the local seed; check the "projects" list for ids on AWS.
@projectId = 1

### Health: the only public route. Proves CloudFront -> Lambda -> database is up.
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Log in as the admin (AD000001). Admin sees everything, including the audit log.
# @name login
# @prompt password Admin password (AD000001)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "AD000001",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Who am I: the user record behind the token (role is re-read from the database).
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Q1 status of each project, Q2 at risk, Q7 budget: dashboard cards, at-risk first.
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Q2 projects at risk of missing deadlines, each with its reasons.
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard/at-risk
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Q3 resource allocation and Q5 over-allocated people: people x weeks, only those over capacity.
GET {{baseUrl}}/dashboard/allocation?overOnly=true&weeks=8
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Q1 project list: search and status filter, paginated (items, page, pageSize, total, totalPages).
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects?status=ACTIVE&page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Q7 budget consumed versus planned, for one project.
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/budget
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Q4 key deliverables and completion, for one project.
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/milestones
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Q6 dependency chain between deliverables: nodes and edges for one project.
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/dependency-graph
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Pull board for one project: tasks with a status, an assignee, who holds how many (held / limit).
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/board
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Ready tasks the signed-in employee could take, with their held / limit. Employees only:
# as the admin this answers 403, so log in as an employee (for example Ana) to try it.
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/ready-tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Requests you may decide, pending only. scope: MINE (you asked) or TO_DECIDE; also kind=.
# Admins decide every request; a manager decides their own employees' requests.
GET {{baseUrl}}/project-requests?scope=TO_DECIDE&status=PENDING
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Requests of one kind: NEW_PROJECT, ARCHIVE_PROJECT, TASK_LIMIT, OVERTIME or OTHER.
# Sending one is a write (POST /project-requests), so it is not here. The body per kind:
#   manager:  {"kind": "NEW_PROJECT", "name": "Hermes", "justification": "...",
#              "proposedStart": "2026-11-01", "proposedEnd": "2027-02-28"}
#   manager:  {"kind": "ARCHIVE_PROJECT", "projectId": 1, "justification": "..."}
#   employee: {"kind": "TASK_LIMIT", "taskLimit": 3, "justification": "..."}
#   employee: {"kind": "OVERTIME", "justification": "..."}
#   either:   {"kind": "OTHER", "name": "A second monitor", "justification": "..."}
GET {{baseUrl}}/project-requests?kind=OVERTIME
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Audit log, newest first (admin only). Every change, with before/after state.
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/audit-log?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Audit log filtered: only changes to projects, on or after a date.
# Filters: actorId, entityType (projects, milestones, assignments, tasks, time_entries,
# users, project_requests), entityId, dateFrom, dateTo (YYYY-MM-DD).
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/audit-log?entityType=projects&dateFrom=2026-10-13
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Notifications for the signed-in user (the bell), unread only.
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications?unread=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The number on the bell.
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Logged time waiting for approval (feeds consumed cost, Q7, once approved).
GET {{baseUrl}}/approvals/time-entries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### People: search and role filter (managers and admins only).
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?role=EMPLOYEE
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Integrity check (admin only): the 5 invariant queries. Healthy = every list empty.
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/integrity-check
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
